  "overview": "Teensy boards pack an absurd amount of processing power into a footprint smaller than a stick of gum — the 4.0 runs its ARM Cortex-M7 at 600 MHz, making it one of the fastest hobbyist-programmable boards available, and it's fully usable straight from the Arduino IDE via the Teensyduino add-on. It has no bootloader button and no bare programming header exposed by default; instead it uses its own USB-based loader utility. Most pins support several hardware peripherals simultaneously (multiple UARTs, SPI buses, I2C buses, and very high-frequency PWM), which is exactly the kind of headroom demanding real-time robotics or audio-processing projects need.",
  "simpleSummary": "A tiny but extremely fast microcontroller board, usable straight from the Arduino IDE.",
